] [17592186531536 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531536 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531536 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186531380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531536 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531536 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531536 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186530872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531536 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dfeef9c0-222d-580e-9176-2a58212a74b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186531029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186531039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186531149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186531317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531539 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531539 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531539 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186531317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531539 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e749236f-06ab-5ec0-b55c-1658240128bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531573 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531573 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531573 #edb/ref 1069 "q-336597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531573 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531573 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & {e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & -2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-{e}^{-4t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{5}{4}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531573 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "29e3e5d7-28ea-5e8a-b874-caa92a5ebba1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531573 #edb/ref 1074 "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & {e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & -2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4t}\\cdot (-2{e}^{2t})-0\\cdot {e}^{2t}}[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{2t} & -{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{-{e}^{-6t}}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{2t} & -{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-4t} & {e}^{-4t} \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]. \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-4t} & {e}^{-4t} \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-4t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-4t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int -{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -2{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & {e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & -2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531596 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531596 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531596 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531596 #edb/ref 1069 "q-336703" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531596 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531596 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531596 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59d9272b-7eb2-549a-868b-86d14c7fdef5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531596 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into $\\text{initial system of ODEs}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{pre-multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531674 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186531681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531674 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "25f637fb-d499-5964-98b0-d92aa3739826" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531674 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186365800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531679 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186531674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531679 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2cb68189-e6bd-50df-bf7a-85be4d333c8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531679 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186531596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531681 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186531715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531681 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3431c228-5dc1-5a6b-90ef-eb4019f30372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531681 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186311821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531715 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c5d20bf1-c67d-533b-b7e7-2dfd3e6fc008" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531715 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186365808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531717 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186531679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531717 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cef5da74-9e1b-5ac0-acde-a39773d01fea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531717 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186531573 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
